<p>The United States says it will ease certain restrictions to allow Venezuelan oil to be resold to Cuba’s private sector for commercial and humanitarian purposes — a shift that could help ease fuel shortages, according to reports. Reuters said the US Treasury Department framed the move as a targeted easing, announced as Cuba struggles with a severe energy crunch.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ZqJW-nbV614CK6_CqH9DqRAsFpwRGCRM5bBqMvw9zVhTto0QFXYu7dQNdleAbb1Fp_OVVL8fAQpi4YCqvGeCNXXC9jCAIJ6HxitGolCmrAumyB6xSmY8_S_OgDSVnUZGrhEXJbNco3ywQnnr_PB3Ub7CkNPYvYf4VW_uuYSNICTlPZxTTTbK7RNuG6L9gRq_ug5rH1m0V5sxmAZRgbc658BnvyKz5REpgGWbHDbyvyMQF1vFkUipYffiz3X-V2gfhOQoFMc_96-3i3i7Qg' alt='FILE PHOTO: Oil platforms and pumpjacks at Lake Maracaibo, in Cabimas, Venezuela, January 26, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>US authority: The US Treasury Department announced the change, easing certain restrictions so Venezuelan oil can be resold to Cuba’s private sector for commercial and humanitarian purposes, Reuters reported.</li><li>Regional diplomacy: The move landed as top US diplomat Marco Rubio met with Caribbean leaders, according to DW and Al Jazeera.</li><li>Energy squeeze: Cuba’s energy crisis has strained power generation and cut fuel supplies for vehicles, homes, and aviation, the Globe and Mail reported.</li><li>US conditions: Even as it relaxes the oil restrictions, the US is demanding “dramatic” change from Cuba, The Straits Times reported.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US Treasury Department: The US says it will ease certain restrictions to allow Venezuelan oil exports to be resold to Cuba’s private sector for commercial and humanitarian purposes, as the island faces an energy shortage. (<a href='https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/us-allow-resale-venezuelan-oil-cuba-treasury-department-says-2026-02-25/'>Reuters</a>)</li><li>Caribbean neighbors: Caribbean governments warn that worsening conditions in Cuba could deepen a humanitarian crisis and spill over into regional instability, Al Jazeera reported. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/26/us-to-allow-venezuelan-oil-sales-to-cuba-as-alarm-grows-in-the-caribbean'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>US administration (earlier stance): President Trump previously vowed to stop Venezuelan oil from reaching Cuba — a posture DW said helped trigger a crisis on the island before this new easing. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/us-greenlights-resale-of-venezuelan-oil-to-cuba/a-76126101'>DW</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/us-eases-cuba-oil-embargo-but-demands-dramatic-change'>US eases Cuba oil embargo but demands ‘dramatic’ change</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/us-greenlights-resale-of-venezuelan-oil-to-cuba/a-76126101'>US greenlights resale of Venezuelan oil to Cuba</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/business/article-venezuela-oil-cuba-resale-energy/'>U.S. to allow resale of Venezuelan oil to Cuba, Treasury Department says</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1repd1j/us_to_allow_resale_of_venezuelan_oil_to_cuba/'>US to allow resale of Venezuelan oil to Cuba</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/26/us-to-allow-venezuelan-oil-sales-to-cuba-as-alarm-grows-in-the-caribbean'>US to allow Venezuelan oil sales to Cuba as alarm grows in the Caribbean</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/us-allow-resale-venezuelan-oil-cuba-treasury-department-says-2026-02-25/'>The United States announces that it will ease certain restrictions to permit Venezuelan oil exports to Cuba&#x27;s private sector for commercial and humanitarian purposes amid an energy shortage.</a> - reuters.com</li></ul>